maturity gating per §2 R#9, §7.2, §10.5; (8) `mle_stakeholder_reporting` — auto-generates Model Cards, Architecture Comparison Reports, Experiment Reports (with equal-rigor negative results), Weekly Experiment Digest, Per-Incident PIR, Daily Standup Digest, Quarterly Impact Narrative per §4.4, §7.3, §9 (leverages existing atlassian/slack/google_drive/gmail MCPs). TOOLS to create: (a) `ml_lens_query_client` — drift, model-perf, system-health, data-quality dashboard queries; (b) `signalfx_detector_iac` — author/apply detectors-as-code; (c) `rovo_eval_runner` and (d) `aix_eval_runner` — programmatic eval execution; (e) `circuit_breaker_control` — activate/inspect circuit breakers; (f) `finops_cost_query` — ML Artifact Cost Monitoring queries; (g) `orbit_context_client` — read model lineage/experiment history/data-quality signals and write outcome enrichments; (h) `pir_drafter` — produces PIR from reasoning traces with TTD/TTH/TTR/TTC. Existing MCPs reused: `atlassian` (Confluence model cards, Jira incident tickets), `slack` (alerts/war-room), `google_drive`+`gmail` (distribution), `socrates` (data queries for drift/cost), `bitbucket` (rollback PRs). RESEARCH REQUIREMENT: study ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook, responsible-ai-api runbook (OTel sidecar race, tenant burst, gevent saturation, ALB decoupling), SPIKE: ML Evaluation Framework, MLOps@CoreML Long-Term Plan, Agent Budget Guardrails, Agentic Operations in the New SDLC, RFC-002, Policy for AI Agents in SDLC.

**Todos**:
- Inventory ML Lens, SignalFx, JSM Ops, rovo-eval, AIX-eval, FinOps dashboards, ORBIT context layer, and Symphony orchestrator agent-side APIs/SDKs/CLIs.
- Author `ml_observability_and_slo` SKILL.md with drift query patterns (KS/KL/cosine), SLO IaC examples, circuit-breaker tuning, autoscaling, and decoupled health-check patterns from responsible-ai-api.
- Author `drift_triggered_retraining` SKILL.md as SOP-1 runbook with autonomy-tier gating (🟢/🟡/🔴) and ORBIT-append step.
- Author `ml_incident_response` SKILL.md as SOP-3 runbook including the 30-min status cadence, cross-correlation playbook, and PIR auto-draft template referencing TTD<15min and TTR<2h targets.
- Author `ml_evaluation_protocol` SKILL.md encoding the 6-stage protocol and AI-native non-negotiables; cross-link rovo-eval vs AIX-eval selection criteria.
- Author `ml_launch_review_gate` SKILL.md operationalizing the ML Launch Review Checklist as automated gates.
- Author `cost_and_capacity_stewardship` SKILL.md with per-experiment budget enforcement and the SageMaker→TEAMServe ~59% savings migration template.
- Author `symphony_orbit_governance` SKILL.md covering 3-tier autonomy enforcement, ORBIT read/write contract, policy-pack compliance, audit emission, and RFC-002 L1–L5 maturity progression.
- Author `mle_stakeholder_reporting` SKILL.md with templates for Model Card, Experiment Report (equal-rigor negative results), Architecture Comparison Report, Weekly Experiment Digest, Per-Incident PIR, Quarterly Impact Narrative; map distribution targets to existing MCP toolsets.
- For each TOOL listed, validate no existing MCP covers it; document the gap, propose tool surface, and identify auth/scope requirements.
- Specify Day-One Readiness access matrix for observability (ML Lens dashboards + alert author), SignalFx detector authoring, JSM Ops + Slack integration, ORBIT bind, audit log sink.
