Tool Inventory (10 tools): channel_create_message (text/html, threadTs),
slack_create_scheduled_message (Unix postAt, threadTs), message_get_reply
(paginated thread reads), channel_get_message, slack_search_realtime (limit
20, supports in:/from: modifiers), channel_get_members, get_user,
workspace_search_user_by_email, slack_create_channel_invite, check_permission
(read-only).

Workflow Coverage:

 • ✅ 30-min status cadence: achievable via create_scheduled_message
   re-scheduling loop with threadTs for threading.
 • ✅ Ack-in-seconds: achievable but only via client-side polling of
   message_get_reply — no push/blocking primitive.
 • ✅ Cross-channel broadcast of Model Card / Experiment Digest / Quarterly
   Narrative using contentType=html.
 • ✅ Bridge channel formation via slack_create_channel_invite (requires
   pre-provisioned channel).
 • ✅ Symphony Tier-1/2/3 posting + read-back of human confirmations.

Critical Gaps (need new tools from Subtask 2):

 1 slack_wait_for_ack — server-side blocking wait with timeout/escalation
   (replaces wasteful polling; rate-limit safe). Most impactful gap.
 2 cancel_scheduled_slack_message — no Slack-side cancel; scheduled cadence
   reminders cannot be killed when incident resolves early.
 3 slack_update_message — no chat.update; status blocks/digests cannot be
   edited.
 4 slack_add_reaction / get_reactions — emoji ACK pattern unusable.
 5 slack_post_blocks (Block Kit) — no interactive ACK buttons.
 6 slack_upload_file — cannot attach Model Card PDFs.
 7 slack_create_channel — incident bridge channels must be pre-provisioned.

Integration Patterns: Slack ↔ Jira (parse CTSC-xxxxx from thread replies),
Slack ↔ Confluence (PIR doc populated from message_get_reply), Slack ↔
Bitbucket (PR merge triggers next thread reply), Slack ↔ Socrates (SQL → html
digest).

AI-Autonomy: All reads autonomous; channel_create_message autonomous for
ops/alert channels but confirm for exec/stakeholder channels;
create_channel_invite always confirm.

Constraints: tier-3 rate limit ~50 req/min; 120-day max for scheduled messages
(quarterly narrative OK, annual not); threadTs must be string-preserved to
keep microsecond precision; search index lags real-time (unsuitable for
ack-in-seconds).


