                   Key extractions from the role definition

§6 SOP-2 (verbatim 9-step sequence with autonomy tiers):

  1 🟡 Confirm problem framing + non-goals with PM.
  2 🟢 Auto literature survey (≥3 papers + ≥2 prior internal experiments).
  3 🟢 Pre-analysis notebook (data sources, label strategy, validation
    methodology).
  4 🟢 Proactive data-quality audit (coverage/sparsity/freshness per
    connector/region/tenant) before training — this is the cross-link to
    feature_store_lifecycle.
  5 🟢 Parallel design — 5–10 variants fully trained, not benchmarked.
  6 🟢 Mandatory ablation with interactions quantified, not just isolated
    contributions.
  7 🟢 Comprehensive error analysis on every failure case; slice by all
    dimensions.
  8 🟡 Recommendation with confidence bounds, rejected alternatives + reasons,
    expected production impact.
  9 Handoff to SOP-1 deploy phase.

§4.3 MLflow Model_<TS> spec: standardized run name pattern, flattened param
logging (nested dicts → .-separated keys), per-segment metric logging,
mlflow.<framework>.log_model for artifacts. <TS> format not pinned by role def
— recommend UTC YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ; variant suffix Model_<TS>__<variant>,
ablation suffix __abl_<component>.

§4.2 Non-negotiables (mechanical gates): failure-case taxonomy {data quality,
model limitation, feature gap, label noise, distribution shift}; mean±std
across multiple seeds (reject single-seed); full k-fold
(stratified/timeseries/group); discrimination + calibration + CIs + fairness
checks.

§10.2 Six elevated standards: Exhaustive HPO to statistical convergence
(Optimus Prime); perfect documentation incl. equal-rigor negative results;
rigorous ablations with interaction quantification; comprehensive error
analysis pre-deploy; zero technical debt; "always the proper solution" (never
single-seed, never test-set HP selection, never temporal/group leakage, always
rejected alternatives).

§3.4 Soft competencies shaping voice: calibrated uncertainty, bias-free
judgment ("don't use ML" is valid), measured-vs-inferred discipline,
cumulative ORBIT learning.

Feature audit cadence (Cluster B / §2 row 4 + SOP-2 step 4): continuous +
on-demand pre-training; triad of {coverage, freshness (p50/p95/max age),
sparsity}; sliced by connector × region × tenant; autonomy 🟢 consume/extend,
🟡 new pipeline, 🔴 schema change affecting consumers.


                          Tool surface implications

 • mlflow_run_manager — create_run(Model_<TS>), log_flattened_params,
