## 6. Python SDK — `atlassian_ml_lens_sdk`

### Installation & Location
Package: `atlassian-ml-lens-sdk`
Source: `atlassian/ml-studio/libraries/.../atlassian_ml_lens_sdk`

### Core Objects

**MetricsPayload dataclass:**
```python
@dataclass(frozen=True)
class MetricsPayload:
    metric_namespace_and_key: str        # e.g., "kyc.reranking.NDCG@1"
    type: str                            # "number", "string", or "boolean"
    value: Any# the measured number
    timestamp: Optional[Union[str, int, float]] = None
    source_type: Optional[str] = None
    tags: Dict[str, Any] = field(default_factory=dict)
```

### Usage Pattern — Emitting Metrics:
```python
from atlassian_ml_lens_sdk.client.ml_lens_client import MlLensClient
from atlassian_ml_lens_sdk.client.models import MetricsPayload
from atlassian_ml_lens_sdk.metrics.metrics import send_metrics

client = MlLensClient()

payloads = [
    MetricsPayload(
        metric_namespace_and_key="namespace.evaluation_metric.mean",
        type="number",
        value=1.23,
        tags={"env": "dev"}
    ),
]

send_metrics(
    run_id="example-run-id",
    metrics=payloads,
    client=client,
)
```

### Key SDK Methods:
- `MlLensClient()` — creates client instance
- `send_metrics(run_id, metrics, client)` — batch emit metrics
- `client.get_aggregated_metric(metric, filter_by, resolution_type, roll_up)` — **being added** (wraps `/api/v1/metrics/aggregated-analysis/{namespace.key}`)

### SDK Alert Configuration:
```python
AlertConfig(alert_namespace="my-team.features", alert_key="drift").alert_message("Drift detected in feature distributions.")
    .runbook("https://...").alert_config(
        AlertMetricConfig(metric_namespace="feature_observability.drift.ks_pvalue")
        .condition(AlertCondition.single(Condition(measure="expected_value", operator="<=", value=0.05)))
        .tag_filter("feature_name", "=", "daily_transaction_count")
        .tag_filter("feature_service", "=", "fraud_detection_v2")
    )
    .recipient(Recipient.slack(RecipientValue(id="#ml-alerts", type="channel")))
```

**Source**: [ML Lens: How it works](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/6973026460), [ML Studio ML Lens Evaluation Metrics](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/6078891934)

