## Finding 2: Assistance-Service-Eval (ASE) — Legacy Platform (Maintenance Mode)

### What it is
A Kotlin-based Micros service (`assistance-service-eval`) that provides a web UI and REST API for running evaluations of Rovo Chat skills, tools, plugins, and agents. Accessible at `go/rovoeval`.

### How it works

**Architecture:**
- Hosted as a Micros service (Tier 3)
- Kotlin codebase
- Two instances: production tenants and staging tenants
- Sends prompts through the actual convo-ai stack end-to-end
- Runs "calculators" (evaluation functions, some LLM-as-judge) against results
- Supports single-turn and multi-turn conversation evaluation
- A/B testing via Switcharoo/Statsig feature flags
- Daily automated runs via Cronman

**REST API Surface:**
```
POST {assistance-service-eval.target-url}/api/v1/metric/success-metric-live# Synchronous eval
POST {assistance-service-eval.target-url}/api/v1/metric/success-metric        # Async eval (fire-and-forget)
POST /api/v1/human-eval/campaigns                             # Create human eval campaign
GET/api/v1/human-eval/campaigns/{campaignId}                                # Get campaign
POST /api/v1/human-eval/campaigns/{campaignId}/assign# Assign evaluators
GET  /api/v1/human-eval/campaigns/{campaignId}/results                        # Get results
POST /api/v1/human-eval/tasks# Create eval tasks
GET  /api/v1/human-eval/evaluators/{evaluatorId}/tasks                        # Get assigned tasks
POST /api/v1/human-eval/tasks/{taskId}/complete# Complete task
```

**Typical Workflow:**
1. Create dataset (JSON format with `source`, `input`, `reference answers`)
2. Upload dataset to the platform
3. Create new experiment (select dataset, calculators, agent, environment)
4. Submit — runs via SQS queue (online) or local IDE (local)
5. View results in dashboard

**Auth Configuration (`.secrets.json`):**
```json
{
  "BOT_USER_NAME": "rovo-eval-bot",
  "BOT_USER_ID": "712020:b8f8b092-376b-4fe0-8ecd-c21c45f2eac3",
  "BOT_API_ACCOUNT": "your.email@atlassian.com",
  "BOT_API_TOKEN": "<your-atlassian-api-token>",
  "BOT_USER_CONTEXT_TOKEN": "<your-user-context-jwt-token>"
}
```

**ConvoAI API Called by ASE:**
```
POST /api/rovo/v1/chat/conversation/{conversationId}/message/stream
```
With headers: `Atl-Cloudid`, `X-Experience-Id`, `X-Product`, `User-Context` (UCT)

**Multi-Turn Support (via ASE):**
- Uses `api/csm/v2/chat/simulate/channel/{conversationId}/message/stream` endpoint
- Leverages `DialogueCreateHistoryItemRequestMapper` for chat history
- Request includes `dialogues: List<Dialogue>` field
- Multi-turn dataset format supports conversation turns array

**Limitations (why it's in maintenance mode):**
- Heavy local stack (Nebulae + Java21+ Docker),30-60 min onboarding
- Kotlin-only codebase (harder to extend metrics)
- Non-compliant database for customer data
- Non-tenanted application layer
- Requires specific end-user bot accounts
- No operational maturity (Tier 3)

### How it applies
ASE is being superseded by Stratus Evals SDK for new work. The `rovo_eval_runner` tool should primarily target the Stratus SDK, but may need a legacy adapter for accessing existing ASE datasets and historical experiment results.

### Source
- [Assistance Service Eval (ASE)](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203bd0205883eb4c12af95fe0e997be99f/pages/6521958926)
- [HOWTO: Run Convo-ai Evaluations on Assistance-service-eval](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202059c7c343a28e46519c83221e3ace599c/pages/5917873802)
- [Modifications made: Run convo-ai and assistance-service-eval platform locally](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020fb66381743f94b398e9ae45493168b8a/pages/6411602966)

