## Finding 4: AURA-Eval REST API (Internal Agent Evaluation Service)

### What it is
An internal REST API used by the Aura team for agent quality measurement, providing batch evaluation capabilities with metrics like `task_completion`, `tool_correctness`, and `argument_correctness`.

### How it works

**API Surface:**
```
POST /api/v2/evaluate# Single test case (sync)
POST /api/v2/evaluate/batch/sync# Sync batch ≤20 cases
POST /api/v2/evaluate/batch/async                  # Async batch via SQS
GET  /api/v2/evaluate/batch/{run_id}               # Poll async batch status/results

POST /api/v2/eval-sets# Create eval set
GET  /api/v2/eval-sets                             # List eval sets
GET  /api/v2/eval-sets/{eval_set_id}               # Get eval set + test cases
PUT  /api/v2/eval-sets/{eval_set_id}               # Update eval set
DELETE /api/v2/eval-sets/{eval_set_id}# Delete eval set
POST /api/v2/eval-sets/{eval_set_id}/test-cases   # Add test cases

POST /api/v2/agents# Register agent for eval
GET  /api/v2/agents/{agent_id}/runs               # List past runs
GET  /api/v2/agents/{agent_id}/runs/latest        # Most recent run
GET  /api/v2/agents/{agent_id}/runs/{run_id}      # Run details
```

### Source
- [Aura: Eval-Driven Agentic AI Architecture](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AA7/pages/6307624323)
