## Finding 5: Multi-Turn Agent Simulation Patterns

### What it is
The multi-turn evaluation capability uses "User Simulator" agents to generate realistic multi-turn conversations with Rovo agents, then evaluates quality across the entire dialogue.

### How it works

**Two Approaches:**

**A. Pre-defined Multi-Turn Datasets (Deterministic):**
- Upload fixed conversation turns as structured JSON
- System replays each turn sequentially, feeding prior turns as history
- Evaluate final response or per-turn quality

**B. User Simulator (LLM-Powered):**
- An LLM simulates realistic user responses based on scenario context
- Generates 5-15 turn conversations
- Methods: `respond_to_question()`, `is_requirements_ready()`, `extract_questions()`
- Supports gradual information disclosure patterns

**ConvoAI Simulation API:**
```
POST api/csm/v2/chat/simulate/channel/{conversationId}/message/stream
```
- Separates simulation traffic from main stream
- Throws exception for `ConversationTypeParam = Real` (safety guard)
- Accepts `dialogues: List<Dialogue>` in request body for chat history

**Multi-Turn Metrics:**
- TaskCompletion (overall conversation goal achieved)
- Groundedness (per-turn)
- Relevance (per-turn)
- Completeness (per-turn)
- Instruction Following (per-turn)
- Tool Use Accuracy (per-turn)

### How it applies
The `rovo_eval_runner` tool needs to support:
1. Fixed multi-turn dataset replay (deterministic, reproducible)
2. Simulated multi-turn generation (for coverage testing)
3. Per-turn and per-conversation metric aggregation

### Source
- [HOWTO: Multi-turn Eval and User Simulator](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/gai/pages/5857806942)
- [Multi turn evaluation DACI](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/H3/pages/5848998020)
- [Multi turn evaluation LLD](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120201a2d2afc5f204e8f93cce0159800ea73/pages/5559515929)

