## Finding 7: Result Retrieval Patterns

### What it is
Multiple mechanisms for retrieving evaluation results depending on the system used.

### How it works

**Stratus Evals SDK (Local):**
- Results written to `results/<timestamp>-eval/` directory
- Formats: JSONL (per-task), `metrics.json` (aggregate), `report.html` (visual)
- Optional: MLflow experiment tracking + Databricks Unity Catalog upload
- Programmatic access: load JSONL files, join by `task_id` across runs

**Batch Evals (GraphQL):**
```graphql
query {
  agentStudio_batchEvaluationResults(jobRunId: "...") {
    results {
      datasetItemId
      status
      score
      feedback
      conversationId
    }
    summary {
      totalCount
      passedCount
      failedCountresolutionRate
    }
  }
}
```

**ASE Platform:**
- Web UI dashboard at `go/rovoeval`
- Results stored in ERS (Entity Resource Service)
- Daily metric reports via Cronman
- Experiment cloning for A/B comparison

### Source
- [Batch Evals Backend Observability](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/qura/pages/6159084608)
- [Analytics Dashboard](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/fde/pages/6869956337)

