## 9. Existing MCP Coverage — Gap Analysis

### What it is
The Splunk Observability Cloud MCP Server provides a 12-tool read-only surface. This analysis identifies what the `signalfx_detector_iac` tool needs that isn't covered.

### How it works (existing MCP tools)

| # | Tool | Capability |
|---|------|-----------|
| 1 | `generate_signalflow_program` | LLM-generated SignalFlow |
| 2 | `execute_signalflow_program` | Run SignalFlow (read-only) |
| 3 | `get_metric_names` | Search metrics catalog |
| 4 | `get_metric_metadata` | Get metric dimensions |
| 5 | `search_alerts_or_incidents` | Query alerts |
| 6-12 | APM tools | Service topology, latency, errors |

**Gap**: All 12 tools are **read-only**. No `create_detector`, `update_detector`, `delete_detector`, `mute_detector` tools. The MCP server intentionally does not wrap mutation endpoints.

**Source**: [ICC Telemetry — MCP Server Investigation Findings](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/6972699425)

### How it applies
- `signalfx_detector_iac` fills a **clear gap**: no existing MCP tool covers detector authoring/lifecycle
- The existing MCP's `execute_signalflow_program` could be reused for validation, but the IaC tool needs to own:
  - `.tf` file generation (author)
  - Terraform plan/apply orchestration
  - Sauron integration
  - Detector state inspection beyond what the read-only MCP provides

