## 10. Standard File/Folder Structure

### What it is
Atlassian teams follow a consistent pattern for organizing SignalFx Terraform code.

### How it works

```
repo-root/
├── .sauron.yml                          # Sauron config (MUST be at root)
├── bitbucket-pipelines.yml              # CI/CD with Sauron step
└── operations/terraform/                # or terraform/ or metrics/sauron/
    ├── main.tf                          # Provider, module imports
    ├── variables.tf# Global variables
    ├── sauron.tf                        # Backend + provider (Sauron-managed)
    ├── locals.tf                        # Notification configs, shared values
    ├── modules/
    │   ├── dashboards/
    │   │   └── *.tf
    │   └── detectors/
    │       ├── detector.<name>.tf       # One file per detector (or group)
    │       └── variables.tf
    └── terraform.tfvars.example         # Example local config
```

**Naming conventions**:
- Detector files: `detector.<name-of-detector>.tf`
- Detector resource names: descriptive snake_case (NOT `A`, `B`)
- Detector display name: `${var.resource_name_prefix} <title>`
- Detect labels: `(env) <detection rule name>` — must include environment if applicable

**Source**: [HOWTO: Create a custom SFX Detector in IS](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/actionsservice/pages/5829842368), [Getting Started: Manage SignalFX Resources with Sauron](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/afm/pages/6177874524)

