## 9. Implementation Pattern Recommendation

### Dual-layer control architecture
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  circuit_breaker_control tool           │
├──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Layer 1:     │ Switcheroo/Statsig API                   │
│ Feature Gate │ • aiops_circuit_breaker_enabled│
│              │ • Environment/tenant targeting            │
│              │ • No-deploy toggle                       │
├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Layer 2:     │ Admin REST Endpoint (per-pod)            │
│ State Control│ • GET /admin/circuit-breaker/ml-engine   │
│              │ • POST /admin/circuit-breaker/transition  │
│              │ • PUT /admin/circuit-breaker/config       │
├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Layer 3:     │ SignalFx + Splunk Queries                │
│ Observability│ • resilience4j_circuitbreaker_* metrics  │
│              │ • State transition logs                   │
└──────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Auth requirements
- **Switcheroo API**: Requires Atlassian SSO + team membership for gate modification
- **Admin endpoint**: Requires in-cluster access (via `atlas micros` role assume or PoCo allow-list)
- **SignalFx/Splunk**: Requires org token or SAML auth for read access

### Key insight: No existing MCP tool covers this
None of the existing MCP tool surfaces (atlassian, bitbucket, google_*, slack, socrates, compass) provide circuit breaker management. The gap is:
- No Switcheroo/Statsig management API in existing MCP tools
- No Resilience4j admin endpoint wrapper
- No SignalFx metrics query for CB state
- This is a net-new tool requirement

