## 2. Control Mechanism — Feature Gate (Switcheroo/Statsig)

### What it is
The ML-Engine CB is gated behind a **Switcheroo feature gate** named `aiops_circuit_breaker_enabled`. This gate determines whether the circuit breaker logic is active.

### How it works
1. **Gate name**: `aiops_circuit_breaker_enabled`
2. **Gate URL**: `https://switcheroo.atlassian.com/ui/gates/14ae760c-ba0f-4f8f-a62d-1ecd169737f1/key/aiops_circuit_breaker_enabled`
3. **Targeting attributes**:
   - `environment` — targets specific regions (prod-west2, prod-east, etc.)
   - `service` attribute = `ML_ENGINE` — scopes to ml-engine service only
4. **Rollout strategy**: Region-by-region starting from `prod-west2` (hello tenant)

### Override semantics
- **Disable CB globally**: Turn off the Switcheroo gate → immediate effect, no deploy required
- **Disable CB for specific tenants**: Add override rule in Statsig with `tenantId` targeting → `100% Fail`
- **Re-enable CB**: Remove the override or set rule to `100% Pass`

### How it applies to `circuit_breaker_control` tool
The tool needs a command to **toggle the feature gate** via the Switcheroo/Statsig API surface. This provides the "activate/deactivate" semantics at the macro level.

### Source
- [ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook — Quick Links](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/6058351626/ML-Engine+Circuit+Breaker+Runbook)
- [Circuit Breaker: Ml-engine & Firebolt — Release Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~185648802/pages/5684132441/Circuit+Breaker+Ml-engine+Firebolt)

