## 1. Overview & Identity

**What it is**: AIX-eval (package name: `atlassian-ai-experience-evaluation`, also known as `aixeval`) is Atlassian's internal Python-based LLM evaluation framework developed by the AI Experience (AIX) team. It is Atlassian's most mature internal evaluation framework, with1.9k+ accumulated downloads, 110+ evaluation metrics contributed, and 13+ AI features onboarded across 11+ projects.

**Package**: `atlassian-ai-experience-evaluation` (available in Atlassian private Artifactory)
**Repository**: `bitbucket.org/atlassian/ai-experience-evaluation` (main branch)
**ML Studio Module**: `bitbucket.org/atlassian/ml-studio/src/main/modules/src/ai_experience/aixeval_run/`
**Slack Channel**: `#help-ai-experience`

**Source**: [AIX-Eval Overview](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203bd0205883eb4c12af95fe0e997be99f/pages/6522081308/AIX-Eval), [AIX Evals Status Quo & Gap Analysis](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/fde/pages/6983520444/AIX+Evals+Status+Quo+Gap+Analysis)

---

## 2. Three Operational Modes (Execution Model)

AIX-eval supports three distinct operational modes:

### Mode 1: `evaluate`
- **Purpose**: Run evaluation metrics against a dataset with pre-existing LLM outputs
- **Input**: DataFrame (CSV, Parquet, Spark table) with `input`, `output`, and optionally `reference` columns
- **Processing**: Metrics are computed per-row via `async compute_on_row(row: pd.Series)` — stateless and independent
- **Output**: DataFrame with appended metric score columns

### Mode 2: `generate`
- **Purpose**: Generate LLM responses based on custom model settings, prompts, and configurations
- **Input**: DataFrame with an input column + prompt templates (Jinja2 or Python) + model configuration
- **Processing**: Calls AI Gateway (or other configured client) to generate responses for each row
- **Output**: DataFrame with an additional response/output column

### Mode 3: `optimise` (ALPO - Algorithmic Prompt Optimization)
- **Purpose**: Run automated prompt optimization using the ALPO framework (based on APO - Automated Prompt Optimization)
- **Input**: Dataset, initial prompt, metric to optimize for, custom error collection function, gradient prompt, candidate-generation prompt
- **Processing**: Iteratively tunes prompts using feedback loops, scoring candidates via specified metrics
- **Output**: Top `n` optimized prompts that perform best for the primary metric

**Source**: [AIX Evals Status Quo & Gap Analysis](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/fde/pages/6983520444/AIX+Evals+Status+Quo+Gap+Analysis), [A Deep Dive into AI Quality Improvement Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AM3/pages/4157214981/A+Deep+Dive+into+AI+Quality+Improvement+Framework+from+AIX+team)

