## Finding 6: Cost Attribution Framework & MOI

### What it is
The Metrics of Interest (MOI) framework provides fine-grained cost attribution for shared resources by tracking consumption signals.

### How it works

**MOI Architecture:**
- Services emit usage metrics (tokens, API calls, bytes, compute hours)
- FinOps Input Attribution System (IAS) uses MOIs to split shared costs
- Data lives in `cloud_finops_ias.moi_cost_attribution_result_platform` and `*_product` tables

**MOI Naming Convention:**
```
{domain}.{service}.{api}.{unit}
```
Example: `identity.perms.bulkPermitted.per-1k`

**Key MOI for ML:**
- `ml-studio-usecase-78c8ff56` — ML Studio per-use-case attribution
- `ai-gateway-8f5269af` — AI Gateway direct attribution

**Dimensions tracked:**
- `caller_app_id`, `product`, `flow`, `api_method`, `region`, `environment`, `tenant`
- For AI: `service_name`, `use_case_id`, `model_id`, `cost_category`

**Ingestion patterns:**
- Preference: Use built-in connectors (Splunk, Socrates, SignalFx) to push aggregated usage
- Hourly aggregation by default, daily rollup with 365-day retention
- MOI REST endpoint only for edge cases

### How it applies
The `finops_cost_query` tool can leverage MOI data to show attributed cost per experiment, especially for shared infrastructure (e.g., "how much of the AI Gateway cost is attributable to my use case?"). The query pattern:

```sql
SELECT *
FROM production.cloud_finops_ias.moi_cost_attribution_result_platform
WHERE client_identifier LIKE '%{use_case_id}%'
    AND period BETWEEN '{start}' AND '{end}'
```

### Source
- [Cost Attribution Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120202c3547288e064fd8844ea7fd4efa1698/pages/5917327397)
- [AI Cost Attribution & Allocation Design](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CFINOPS/pages/6407688137)
- [Enhance LLM consumption metrics for AI cost allocation (COMMIT-26340)](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/COMMIT-26340)

