## Finding 8: OpenAI Cost Ingestion (AI Gateway Stats)

### What it is
The AI Gateway ingests cost data from LLM vendors (primarily OpenAI) and publishes it as a SignalFx metric and into Socrates tables.

### How it works

**Metric:** `mlp.ai-gateway.cost.openai`
- Published to SignalFx, powers cost charts at `go/aigatewaysfx`
- Implemented as AI Gateway Stats Socrates data product
- Orchestrated via Airflow DAG (hourly schedule)
- Queries OpenAI Cost API, aggregates daily costs

**Data Flow:**
```
OpenAI Cost API → Airflow DAG → Socrates data product → SignalFx metric→ cost_table_consume (Databricks)
```

**Repo:** Bitbucket — AI Gateway Stats data product

### How it applies
For per-experiment budget queries related to LLM costs:
- The `cost_table_consume` table provides token-level granularity with `use_case_id` and `service_name`
- The SignalFx metric `mlp.ai-gateway.cost.openai` can be used for real-time alerting
- The tool should be able to query both historical (Socrates) and near-real-time (SignalFx) cost data

### Source
- [HOWTO: Ingest OpenAI Cost as Metric and Push to SFX](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6152569451)

