─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Covered (~80% of SOP-3):

 • Branch cut from a known-good SHA → bitbucketRepoContent 
   action=branch.create (with target).
 • Authoring revert commit → commit.create (files, branch, parents, author
   must be "Name <email>" or 400).
 • Reading prior file content → files.get with referenceOrSha.
 • Default reviewers excluding agent → bitbucketRepository 
   action=defaultReviewers excludeCurrentUser=true.
 • Commit "greenness" gating → getReportListForCommit / getReportForCommit /
   getReportAnnotationsForCommit.
 • Full PR lifecycle → bitbucketPullRequest actions create (supports draft,
   reviewers:[{uuid}], closeSourceBranch), edit, get, list, merge
   (mergeStrategy), approve, comment (parentCommentId, pending), comments,
   diff.
 • Custom rollback pipeline trigger → bitbucketPipeline action=run with
   target/selector/variables; logs via step.log.

Gaps requiring a Subtask-2 tool:

 1 No deployment trigger/promote — bitbucketDeployment is read-only.
 2 No native git-revert; agent must reconstruct file contents (brittle for
   binaries/renames).
 3 No tag/branch.delete/force-push (blocks Symphony L1–L3 release tagging and
   emergency wipe).
 4 No webhook/event subscription — must poll PR action=get (Agent Budget
   Guardrails concern).
 5 No PR-level Code Insights write — drift KS/KL/cosine reports must downgrade
   to free-text comments.
 6 No pipeline cancel/stop (Circuit Breaker can't halt deploys).
 7 commit.create.files is string→string only — binary model-card artefacts
   unsupported.
 8 No cross-repo/fork PRs; no branch-permission introspection (RFC-002 L1–L5
   gating).

Integration patterns: Bitbucket composes with atlassian (Jira-driven
rollback), socrates (drift SQL → PR comment), slack (manual notify), gmail
(PIR distribution). All notifications are agent-mediated; no native event
egress.

Autonomy mapping (RFC-002): L1–L3 use draft=true; L4 pre-stages a rollback
branch for fast merge; L5 enables direct merge but Subtask-2 must enforce
freeze-window checks.

Recommendation: Subtask-2 should ship a rollback_pr orchestrator wrapping the
existing primitives and supplying deployment.promote, true git revert,
tag.create, pipeline.cancel, PR-level Code Insights write, and webhook-driven
PR-state waits.


