## Finding 3: Experiment History via ML Registry + ML Lens

### What It Is
**ML Registry** provides asset management, metadata/lineage tracking, and deployment support. Combined with **ML Lens** (observability), it provides experiment metrics, version history, and annotations.

### How It Works

**ML Registry Capabilities:**
- Component types: prompts, models, datasets, tables, sagemaker-packages
- Versioning of all components
- Annotations (additional metadata attachable to any version)
- ML Lifecycle Notifications (events on version creates, artifact uploads)
- Lineage tracking integration with Dreamcatcher

**Registry Roadmap:**
- Model Deployments tracked in lineage (TEAMserve, Launchpad, Sagemaker)
- Performance profiling reports attached to deployment versions
- Evaluation datasets linked to model versions

**ML Lens Training Observability:**
- Training job log management
- Experimental metrics management and monitoring
- Performance profiler for debugging
- Workflow operational monitoring
- Run comparison across experiments

**ML Lens Metrics Store API:**
```yaml
POST /api/v1/runRequest: { "environment": "prod", "namespace": "abc" }
  Response: { "run_id": "string" }

POST /api/v1/metrics
  Request: PublishMetricRequest (metric definitions, expectations, anomaly configs)

POST /api/v1/runs/metrics
  Request: RunMetricsRequest (metrics for a specific run)
```

**ML Lens SDKs:**
- **ML Lens SDK** (Python) — emits any metric value into metric store via StreamHub
- **Data Quality SDK** (`atlassian-ml-dq-sdk`) — computes quality metrics on PySpark DataFrames and emits to ML Lens
- **MLFlow → ML Lens egress** (in progress) — auto-sync `mlflow.log_metric()` to ML Lens

**Alert Configuration Example:**
```json
{
  "metric_key": "row_count_for_confluence_page",
  "namespace": "abc",
  "type": "row_count",
  "expectations": [
    { "operator": ">=", "expected_value": 900 }
  ],
  "anomaly_detections": [
    { "algorithm": "confidence_band", "config": { "sensitivity": 2} }
  ],
  "alerts": [
    { "type": "jsm_ops", "values": ["eng-ml-platform"] },
    { "type": "slack", "values": ["#ml-platform"] }
  ]
}
```

### How It Applies to the Tool
Commands for experiment history:
- `get_experiment_metrics(workflow_id, run_id)` — query metrics from ML Lens
- `get_model_versions(component_name)` — list versions from ML Registry
- `get_annotations(component_id, version_id)` — get attached annotations
- `compare_runs(run_ids[])` — compare metrics across runs

### Source
- [Registry Roadmap](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5991613386/Registry+Roadmap+High+Level)
- [ML Lens - High Level Architecture](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5546838210/ML+Lens+-+High+Level+Architecture)
- [ML Lens and ML Registry for Experimentation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6408081553)
- [RFC: ML Lens API](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5626083662)

