## Executive Summary

ORBIT at Atlassian refers to **two distinct systems** — (1) the **ORBIT Personalization & Context Layer for Rovo** (the AI/ML ranking platform relevant here) and (2) the **Orbit Developer SDK/Tooling** (inner devloop tooling, not relevant). This research focuses exclusively on #1.

The `orbit_context_client` tool needs to interface with a **constellation of three ML Platform services** that collectively provide model lineage, experiment history, data-quality signals, and outcome enrichment capabilities:

| Capability | Underlying Service | Interface |
|---|---|---|
| Model lineage | **Dreamcatcher** (ML Graph) | GraphQL API via StreamHub events |
| Experiment history | **ML Registry** + **ML Studio** | REST API + ML Lens metrics store |
| Data-quality signals | **ML Lens** | REST API (`/api/v1/metrics`, `/api/v1/runs/metrics`) |
| Ranked context (reading) | **ORBIT Context API** | REST via `collaborator-graph` facade or direct MLFS query |
| Outcome enrichments (writing) | **ORBIT contribution framework** | ML Studio modules → MLFS Feature Store write |

