## Finding 9: Auth & Access Matrix (Day-One Readiness)

| Service | Auth Mechanism | Required Scope/Permission |
|---|---|---|
| ORBIT Context API (`collaborator-graph`) | ASAP token (service-to-service) | Service registered as consumer, purpose declared |
| MLFS Feature Serving | ASAP token | Feature endpoint consumer registration |
| MLFS Feature Write | ASAP token | Namespace owner/delegate grant + component-level WRITE |
| Dreamcatcher (GraphQL) | ASAP token | Read: any authenticated service; Write: publisher policy on StreamHub |
| ML Lens Metrics Store | ASAP token + ML Studio SDK | Namespace ownership for writes, read access for consumers |
| ML Registry | ASAP token | Component read (open), write requires namespace delegation |
| StreamHub (event emission) | Publisher policy registration | Event schema + SQS subscription + publisher consumer policy |

**Key access requirements for the AI employee:**
1. **ORBIT read** — register as a consumer with `AGENT_PLAN` or `AGENT_EXECUTE` purpose
2. **MLFS read** — register service as feature endpoint consumer
3. **Dreamcatcher read** — GraphQL query access (open to authenticated services)
4. **ML Lens read** — access to metrics store (namespace-scoped)
5. **Write enrichments** — MLFS namespace delegation + StreamHub publisher policy

