# pir_drafter Tool Design — Comprehensive Research Findings

## 1. Incident Metrics Definitions & Computation Logic

### 1.1 TTD — Time to Detect

**What it is**: Measures how long it takes an organization to identify a production problem after it starts impacting users.

**How it works** (from [Operational Metrics in Time of Incident - Definitions](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020d1aa82d7378c4a9c8aa92767386e4fa4/pages/3752110446/Operational+Metrics+in+Time+of+Incident+-+Definitions)):
```
TTD = Impact Detection Time - Impact Start Time
```

**Key semantics**:
- "Detecting" means the organization is **aware** of and **acknowledged** the problem
- Detection can be via: monitoring alert, customer report, synthetic check, log anomaly, or vendor notification
- Organizational goals: P80 TTD ≤ 30 minutes for major HOTs; target< 15 minutes per PIR template checklist

**Source timestamps**:
- `impact_start_time`: When users/systems first begin experiencing effects
- `impact_detection_time`: First alert trigger OR first human acknowledgment

**Edge cases** (from [The Case Against Mean TTD](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~aelse/pages/4336344424/The+Case+Against+Mean+TTD)):
- Mean TTD is misleading in isolation; P80 and distribution are preferred
- Some incidents are detected by customers before monitoring, complicating the calculation
- TTD can be negative if detection happens before actual customer impact (proactive)

---

### 1.2 TTH — Time to HOT

**What it is**: Measures elapsed time between impact reaching severity threshold and HOT ticket creation.

**How it works** (from [Changes to Measuring Major Customer Impacting Incidents for FY26](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IMPIR/blog/2025/06/10/5397837113/Changes+to+Measuring+Major+Customer+Impacting+Incidents+for+FY26)):
```
TTH = HOT Creation Time - Sev 2 Breach TimeOR
TTH = HOT Upgrade to Sev 2 Time - Sev 2 Breach Time
```

**Key semantics**:
- FY26 shifted measurement start from initial customer impact to **severity threshold breach**
- This reflects when the incident *should have* escalated to Sev 2
- Often used interchangeably with "Time to HOT" from impact start in older templates

---

### 1.3 TTR — Time to Resolve

**What it is**: Measures total time to fully resolve an incident and restore service.

**How it works** (from [Core Engineering Monthly Operations Review](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CoreEngineering/pages/4159977400/Core+Engineering+Monthly+Operations+review+Incident+metrics+Micros+Engineering+non-Security+Incidents)):
```
TTR = Resolution Time - Impact Start Time
```

**Key semantics**:
- "Resolved" = all previously impacted users are fully restored AND MIM/on-call agrees minimal recurrence risk
- Distinguished from TTM (Time to Mitigate): TTM = when no NEW users are impacted (bleeding stopped), TTR = full resolution
- Organizational goals: P80 TTR ≤ 120 minutes for major HOTs

**FY26 Note**: The L1 KR shifted to TTM (Time to Mitigate) as the primary metric, but TTR is still tracked for PIR action items.

---

### 1.4 TTC — Time to Communicate

**What it is**: Elapsed time between severity escalation and first external customer-facing communication.

**How it works** (from [Calculating TTC](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/6420377152/Calculating+TTC)):
```
TTC = Time of First External Comms - Sev 2 Escalation Time
```

**Key semantics**:
- First comms = first Statuspage update OR first Status Hub posting
- Uses Sev 2 **escalation** time (not breach time) — the actual time the HOT was escalated
- Only measured for L1 KR-impacting scenarios (external customer impact confirmed)
- Target: Within 30 minutes of TTH for covered experiences

**MSR SQL calculation** (from the same source):
```sql
CASEWHEN external_comms.first_external_comms_timestamp IS NOT NULLAND pir.sev_breach_times['2 - Major'] IS NOT NULL
  THEN
    (unix_timestamp(external_comms.first_external_comms_timestamp) 
     - unix_timestamp(pir.sev_breach_times['2 - Major'][0])) / 60
  ...
END AS ttc_mins
```

---

## 2. Input Contract Design

### 2.1 Reasoning Trace Schema

Based on the ICC PRD's data sources table and APIC automation patterns (from [PRD — ICC: Post-Incident Review (PIR)](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/6841106051/PRD+ICC+Post-Incident+Review+PIR) and [APIC: Automated PIR generation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/2937709458/APIC+Automated+PIR+generation+using+Incident+chat)):

