## 6. Existing PIR Automation Patterns (Reference Implementations)

### 6.1 Current APIC System
From [APIC: Automated PIR generation using Incident chat](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/2937709458/APIC+Automated+PIR+generation+using+Incident+chat):
- Triggered by Slack command
- Summarizes incident Slack channel
- Generates automated timeline
- Populates PIR template with action items
- Uses LLM with targeted prompts per section (root cause, mitigation, narrative, metrics, lessons, impact)

### 6.2 Current JSM Automation (A4J)
From [Incident PIR - Automation + AI](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7012112aa5249d2494924bbc5c15c92138367/pages/5536217180/Incident+PIR+-+Automation+AI):
- Trigger: Issue status → "Resolved" or "Closed"
- Creates PIR ticket linked to incident
- Invokes AI PIR component with incident key
- Creates Confluence page with generated content
- Links page to PIR ticket custom field `Document PIR`
- On Loom transcript arrival: triggers PIR update

### 6.3 Post Incident Review Agent (Rovo)
From [Post Incident Review Agent](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121fae44dc7ff064322a11c2c04294ad554/pages/6439324229/Post+Incident+Review+Agent):
- Retrieves incident data from JSM (summary, description, timestamps, status changes)
- Summarizes Microsoft Teams/Slack chat
- Generates PIR with: Executive Summary, Root Cause, Actions & Participants, Resolution, Recommendations
- Formats as Confluence-ready content
- Marks sections where data was insufficient

### 6.4 ICC Phase 1 PIR (Upcoming)
From [PRD — ICC: Post-Incident Review (PIR)](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/6841106051/PRD+ICC+Post-Incident+Review+PIR):
- AI-generated PIR draft from ICC data sources
- Split-pane: timeline (left) + PIR document (right)
- Sections: Incident Summary, Leadup, Fault, Detection, Root Causes, Mitigation & Resolution, Lessons Learnt, Action Items
- AI-generated passages marked with visual indicator
- Data sources: incident timeline, stakeholder comms, RCA hypotheses, mitigation steps, service graph, alert signals, Slack context, change history

