  0 :target-1: Mission Maximize Atlassian teams’ productivity in developing     
  and operating Machine Learning models/pipelines and the value delivered to    
  customers through Machine Learning. 🔭 Vision In the future, Atlassian teams  
  will achieve high productivity in developing and operating Machine Learning   
  models/pipelines. The complexities related to ML data preparation and model   
  training are greatly simplified, all while ensuring strict adherence to data  
  security and privacy policies. Any Atlassian team that wants to create        
  customized AI/ML solutions can utilize an ML purpose-built development        
  platform called ML Studio . ML Studio enables teams to access and prepare     
  high-quality ML datasets, create end-to-end ML workflows, and efficiently     
  conduct numerous experiments. :chess: Strategy To achieve these goals, we     
  aim to follow these strategies: Streamline ML workflows by 1) promoting       
  reusabilities of privacy-compliant datasets, data processing, and training    
  modules; 2) making experimentation as lightweight and iterative as possible;  
  and 3) Integrating with a wide range of advanced AI infrastructures,          
  framework, and open-source models. Strong ML Engineer and platform            
  partnership through cross-team collaborations between Search (representing    
  high-impact and ML-adept team) and ML platform while designing and building   
  ML Studio. image-20240315-105949.png Streamline ML Workflows Current          
  complexities and pain points of ML development in Atlassian arise from the    
  lack of high-quality ML datasets, privacy-compliant and reusable ML workflow  
  building blocks, built-in experimentation support, and powerful AI infra. ML  
  Studio aims to address these challenges by supporting: Reusable and           
  privacy-compliant data/module We aim to minimize the necessity for teams to   
  construct data pipelines from scratch by offering a range of raw,             
  intermediate, and final datasets generated through centralized pipelines.     
  Additionally, ML Studio will decrease the costs of pipeline composition and   
  mitigate privacy violation risks by providing a collection of data            
  processing and training modules that comply with privacy policies. Fast       
  experimentation In real-world ML development, model performance improvements  
  typically arise from rapid experimentation, feature engineering, and model    
  tuning rather than the application of fundamentally different algorithms.     
