## 3. JSM Ops + Slack Integration (for alerting/incident tools)

### Platform Overview
Jira Service Management Operations (formerly Opsgenie) provides alert management, on-call scheduling, and incident response. Integrates with Slack via ChatOps.

### Access Requirements

| Requirement | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Alert API Integration** | Team-level API integration: generates GenieKey (API key) for creating/acknowledging/closing alerts |
| **API Endpoint** | `https://api.atlassian.com/jsm/ops/api/` (Stargate-fronted) |
| **Auth** | GenieKey (integration-level API key, no expiry by design) |
| **Alert Creation** | `POST /v2/alerts` with GenieKey in `Authorization: GenieKey {key}` header |
| **Slack Integration** | Requires: (1) Slack workspace connected to JSM site via Settings > Products > Chat and video tools; (2) Team-level Slack integration created |
| **Webhook Integration** | ForIncidentAI pattern: Webhook integration with `auth-token` custom header + URL endpoint |
| **Roles** | Team Admin in JSM Ops for integration setup; Site Admin for global integrations |
| **Responders** | Can target: `team`, `user`, `escalation`, `schedule` via responder objects |
| **Owner** | JSM Ops Platform team (for integration setup); Team admins (for team-level config) |
| **Request Channel** | Team Operations > Integrations > Add integration; or Settings > Products > Operations > Integrations (global) |
| **Source** | [JSM Ops integration setup guide](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CELLSRE/pages/5058955385), [Integration between JSM ops and signalFx](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020059a75ff71e94e729b894982ee5ac035/pages/5938928396), [JSM Ops Public APIs](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/gold/pages/5958646293) |

### Two API Authentication Paths
1. **User-based API token** (tied to user, with expiry) — for configuration/schedule management
2. **GenieKey** (integration-level, no expiry) — for alert creation from external tools/services

