## 8. PIR Drafter (for `pir_drafter`)

### Platform Overview
Post-Incident Reviews (PIRs) at Atlassian follow a structured process with data in two places: OpsJ PIR ticket (SSoT) and Confluence PIR document (narrative). Key metrics: TTD, TTH, TTR, TTC.

### Access Requirements

| Requirement | Detail |
|---|---|
| **PIR Ticket Access** | OpsJ/Jira — PIR project read access (IRP Jira project) |
| **Confluence PIR Doc** | Auto-created from PIR ticket; read access to PIR Confluence spaces |
| **Incident Data** | HOT tickets in OpsJ; incident timeline events |
| **Metrics Computation** | TTD = detection_time - incident_start; TTR = resolution_time - incident_start; TTH = human_response_time - detection_time; TTC = closure_time - resolution_time |
| **Data Source** | Socrates: `zone_sre` schema (incidents, PIRs, action items); go/incident-metrics (Redash APIs) |
| **Template** | Standard PIR template with: Summary, Timeline, Impact, Causes, Learnings, Actions |
| **Auth** | Jira API access (for PIR tickets); Confluence API access (for PIR docs); Socrates access (for historical data) |
| **Owner** | Reliability Process Group (RPG) |
| **Request Channel** | PIR Champions group; RPG team |
| **Source** | [Post-Incident Reviews (PIRs)](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020569da089a21d46c89d014c3c8a40039d/pages/6272935146), [PIR Checklist](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PFound/pages/4080435575), [How to write an effective PIR](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~880059104/blog/2024/08/20/4075337952) |

### PIR Glossary (for agent understanding)
- **TTD** (Time to Detect): incident_start → first_detection
- **TTR** (Time to Resolve): incident_start → full_mitigation
- **TTH** (Time to Human): detection → first human responder action
- **TTC** (Time to Close): resolution → PIR approved/closed
- **HOT**: Primary incident ticket
- **PIR ticket**: OpsJ issue created post-HOT resolution

---

