## 1. ML Lens (for `ml_lens_query_client`)

### Platform Overview
ML Lens is Atlassian's centralized ML observability platform backed by Observo/StarRocks. It provides metric ingestion, time-series storage, alerting (JSM Ops + Slack), dashboards, and a Query API.

### Access Requirements

| Requirement | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Dashboard Read Access** | Namespace-scoped read access via SSAM access levels; ML Lens creates access levels per registered namespace |
| **Alert Author** | Registration via `POST /api/v1/alerts/register` or Alert Rule V2 API (`POST /api/v1/alerts/rules-v2`) |
| **Query API** | `POST /api/v1/metrics`, `GET /api/v1/metrics/{metrics_key}`, uses ML Lens Query API backed by StarRocks |
| **SDK** | Python SDK: `atlassian_ml_lens_sdk` — `MlLensClient`, `send_metrics()` |
| **Auth Mechanism** | SLAuth (service-to-service); ASAP issuer allowlist for micros services (e.g., `micros/ml-lens` added to SSAM) |
| **Scope** | Namespace-level: agents need namespace registration + read access to relevant metric namespaces |
| **Owner** | ML Platform team (Eng - ML Platform) |
| **Request Channel** | Raise ticket via ML Lens onboarding flow; Slack: `#ml-platform` or `#help-ml-platform` |
| **Source** | [RFC: ML Lens API](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5626083662), [ML Lens Metrics API](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5806815768), [SECASR-7053](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PRODSEC/pages/6962632618) |

### Key APIs
- `POST /api/v1/run` — register validation run
- `POST /api/v1/metrics` — publish metrics
- `GET /api/v1/metrics/{key}` — query metrics
- `POST /api/v1/notifications` — send alerts (Slack/JSM Ops/StreamHub)
- `POST /api/v1/alerts/rules-v2` — create alert rules (V2)

---

## 2. SignalFx (for `signalfx_detector_iac`)

### Platform Overview
Splunk Observability Cloud (SignalFx) is Atlassian's primary monitoring solution. Detectors are managed as Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) via the Terraform `splunk-terraform/signalfx` provider, deployed through Sauron (Bitbucket Pipelines).

### Access Requirements

| Requirement | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Detector Authoring (IaC)** | Shared Terraform token stored in Vault: `observability-users-shared-dl-admin/observability.signalfx.terraform.token.secret` |
| **Dashboard Read** | All Atlassian users get `power` role by default (can view/create dashboards) |
| **Roles** | Two roles: `admin` (Observability team only) and `power` (all Atlassians by default). Lesser roles: `read_only`, `usage` |
| **API Tokens** | User API Access Token (30-day expiry) via profile page; org tokens for services |
| **Token for Pipelines** | Request via OBSHELP ticket — Vault path: `vault://secret/data/builds/observability-users-shared-dl-admin/observability.signalfx.terraform.token.secret` |
| **Auth Header** | `X-SF-TOKEN` header with access token |
| **API Endpoint** | `https://api.us1.signalfx.com` |
| **Terraform Provider** | `splunk-terraform/signalfx` version ~> 6.22.0+ |
| **Sauron Integration** | `.sauron.yml` config in Bitbucket repo; Sauron webhook auto-deploys on merge to main |
| **Owner** | Observability team |
| **Request Channel** | `#observability` Slack channel or raise ticket at go/obshelp (OBSHELP Jira project) |
| **Source** | [How to - SignalFx Config as Code](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/OBSERVABILITY/pages/440445008), [SignalFX SOX ITGC Readiness](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/OTCPSPD/pages/5769005685) |

### Key Considerations for Agent
- Token rotation: Personal tokens expire in 30 days; shared pipeline token can be rotated by Obs team
- Read-only tokens can be issued for metric queries (cannot modify resources)
- SOX compliance concern: `power` role can modify any detector — consider requesting dedicated service token with scoped permissions
- Detector API: `GET /v2/detector/{id}`, `GET /v2/incident`

