## 7. ORBIT Context Client (for `orbit_context_client`)

### Platform Overview
ORBIT is a personalization "context layer" that ranks the most relevant work for each user across Jira, Confluence, Bitbucket, projects, goals, and people/teams. Exposes a Context Pack API.

### Access Requirements

| Requirement | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Context API** | `GET /orbit/context?user={userId}&dimensions=who,what&layers=inner,near&limit=10` |
| **Response** | Structured context pack with ranked entities, reason codes, hydrated metadata, layer tags |
| **Dimensions** | `who`, `what`, `where`, `how` |
| **Layers** | `inner` (active now), `near` (recently touched), `outer` (structural context) |
| **Data Sources** | TwG (Teamwork Graph) relationships, ML Feature Store (MLFS) for ranked scores |
| **Auth** | SLAuth (service-to-service); internal platform API |
| **Status** | In Progress / Planned (as of May 2026) — API may not yet be fully GA |
| **Integration Pattern** | Parallel merge: ORBIT long-term signals + TwG real-time signals |
| **Owner** | ORBIT team (Danny Doan / AI Context & Intelligence) |
| **Request Channel** | Contact ORBIT team; Atlas project ATLAS-118565 |
| **Source** | [ORBIT Platform Strategy](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AICT/pages/7049333779), [ORBIT - Personalization & Context Packaging Layer](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202049b56fb3ef7b49abbbe4f53dbbf12160/pages/6272801311) |

### Key Consideration
ORBIT is still in MVP/development phase. The "bind" operation (registering an agent as a consumer of context packs) requires coordination with the ORBIT team to ensure the agent is registered as an approved consumer with appropriate purpose limits and budgets.

