## Implementation Pattern Recommendation

Based on research into existing MCP implementations at Atlassian:

### Pattern Analysis

| Pattern | Examples | When to Use |
|---------|----------|-------------|
| **TypeScript MCP Server (stdio)** | accelerate-mcp, statuspage-mcp | Local agent tools, simple API wrappers |
| **Platform MCP Tools (integrations-service)** | Jira, Confluence, Bitbucket tools | First-party tools needing consistent auth, auditing |
| **YAML-defined standalone actions** | 3P MCP Tools in IS | Simple CRUD operations |
| **Kotlin-backed complex actions** | Custom IS actions | Complex logic, multi-step flows |

### Recommended Pattern for Each Tool

| Tool | Recommended Pattern | Rationale |
|------|-------------------|-----------|
| `ml_lens_query_client` | TypeScript MCP Server (HTTP) | Read-only queries to ML Lens API; needs ASAP JWT |
| `signalfx_detector_iac` | TypeScript MCP Server (stdio) + CLI wrapper | Wraps Terraform CLI; local state management needed |
| `rovo_eval_runner` | Platform MCP Tool (IS) | Integrates with convo-ai; needs UCT auth |
| `aix_eval_runner` | TypeScript MCP Server (HTTP) | Triggers Databricks/ML Studio jobs; needs workspace auth |
| `circuit_breaker_control` | TypeScript MCP Server (HTTP) | Admin operations; MUST enforce human confirmation |
| `finops_cost_query` | TypeScript MCP Server (HTTP) | Queries FinOps API/Databricks; read-only |
| `orbit_context_client` | Platform MCP Tool (IS) | Core platform integration; needs TWG permission model |
| `pir_drafter` | TypeScript MCP Server (HTTP) + Computation | Multi-source aggregation + metric computation |

### Common Implementation Structure

```typescript
// Standard MCP tool structure (from accelerate-mcp pattern)
import { McpServer } from "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/mcp.js";
import { StdioServerTransport } from "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/stdio.js";
import { z } from "zod";

const server = new McpServer({ name: "tool-name", version: "1.0.0" });

server.tool("command_name", "Description", {
  param1: z.string().describe("..."),
  param2: z.number().optional().describe("..."),
}, async ({ param1, param2 }) => {
  // Auth: ASAP JWT or Bearer token from env
  // Call: underlying API
  // Return: structured result
  return { content: [{ type: "text", text: JSON.stringify(result) }] };
});

const transport = new StdioServerTransport();
await server.connect(transport);
```

### Auth Handling Pattern (from MCP Tool Catalog):

| Auth Mode | Mechanism | Use Case |
|-----------|-----------|----------|
| `oauth` | Atlassian OAuth (3LO) | User-context tools (ORBIT, rovo_eval) |
| `headless-auth` | API key / service account | Infrastructure tools (SignalFx, ML Lens,FinOps) |
| `native` | API token, full tool set | Admin tools (circuit_breaker_control) |

