                       Critical findings (per platform)

ML Studio. Legacy orchestration on Databricks via workflow_descriptor.yml
(tasks, depends_on, platform_override, instance_type). Submission via
Databricks PAT per region. Known gaps: GPU unpredictability, manual MLflow
setup, no native distributed training.

Databricks Jobs API. Python SDK databricks-sdk (WorkspaceClient); REST is Jobs
2.1 (/api/2.1/jobs/runs/submit|run-now|get|cancel|get-output|list). Tokens per
region: DATABRICKS_TOKEN_PROD_{US,EU}_PRODUCER. State enums:
RunLifeCycleState, RunResultState.

ML Fabric (Alpha, May 2026). Argo Workflows + JupyterHub + self-hosted MLflow
+ KFP. URLs: argo|jupyterhub|mlflow.dhbm.kitt-inf.net. In-cluster MLflow URI:
http://mlflow.mlflow:80. GPU = A10G via Karpenter nodepool g5-2x (2–5 min
cold-start). HF token preloaded as mlp-hf-token-secret. Auth is no-cred/dummy
(VPN-gated) in Alpha; SSO is follow-on. Preloaded recipes: quantization,
fine-tuning (LoRA/QLoRA), distillation, mini-pipeline.

MLflow / Model_<TS>. Two backends (Databricks-managed + self-hosted ML
Fabric). Canonical run name
Model_<YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ>__<variant_slug>__abl_<component>. Hard limits:
log_params ≤100 keys/call, value ≤250 chars. Standard idioms: shared
experiment path /Shared/<team>/..., framework-specific
mlflow.<flavor>.log_model, RUN_NOTES dict logged as params+metrics+artifact,
sMAPE+assessment tag (Excellent/Good/Acceptable/Poor/Very Poor).

Optimus Prime HPO. Bayesian (GP-surface) over Databricks Jobs via
mlflow_bayesian_hyperparameter_optimizer.py in atlassian-sa-utils. Contract:
training script reads dbutils.widgets.get("optimizer_parameters") JSON, logs
params + primary metric to MLflow. Recommends max_concurrent_runs ≤ 5,
min_runs ≥ 3×n_dims, replicates for noise estimation.

Tecton/MLFS. Tecton sunsets Feb 16, 2027 (acquired by Databricks). Migration
target = MLFS SDK (com.atlassian.mlp.featurestore:java-client-sdk:0.0.36).
Read API: FeatureStoreService.readFeaturesFromFeatureServiceAsResponse(...)
with joinKeyMap, requestContextMap, latencyBudgetMs. Two patterns: direct SDK
swap (FF-gated FF_ENABLE_READ_FEATURE_FROM_MLFS) OR prediction sidecar
(ml-prediction-sidecar:v1.11.7+). Metrics:
mlfs.sdk.{server,client}.invocation.upper_99. Materialized features exposed in
Socrates zone_tecton.*. MLP UI:
https://ai-platform.services.atlassian.com/ui/ml-studio/features?tab=1. DTIE
interim solution: vNext daily feature pipeline → shared table
(core_ml_data.feature_*) keyed by snapshot_date + entity_key.

Unity Catalog. Production risks: throttling (Sev2 PIR-300964), 10× slower
metadata vs Hive. ML runtimes need single-user access mode. Recommend Socrates
MCP for grant queries; tools must retry on 429s. MLflow tracking is NOT yet
UC-governed; only registered models/tables flow into UC.

GPU quotas. AWS default = 0 for all ml.g5.xlarge|2xlarge, ml.g4dn.xlarge.
Per-region quotas pre-requested (us-east-1: 100, us-west-2/eu/ca: 50,
ap-southeast-1: 2–4). Source-of-truth = SignalFx dashboard GG671nHA0AM (manual
tracking unrealistic).


                           Tool design conclusions


All three Build-side tools (mlflow_run_manager,
mlstudio_databricks_job_launcher, tecton_mlfs_client) are net-new; no existing
MCP toolset covers MLflow tracking, Databricks Jobs, or Tecton/MLFS SDK. Auth
models, REST endpoints, primary ops, Day-One Readiness rows, and cross-tool
SOP-2 chain are documented in §9 of facet.md.
