6-Stage ML Evaluation Protocol (encoded as the canonical SOP for the
ml_evaluation_protocol skill):

 1 Offline → static golden-dataset benchmark (AIX-eval, k-fold + multi-seed)
 2 Adhoc → exploratory probes / ALPO prompt tuning (AIX-eval optimise)
 3 Released → frozen-config re-eval, security/privacy gate (AIX-eval against
   immutable release/)
 4 Packaging → packaged-artifact verification end-to-end through real client
   (rovo-eval / Stratus Evals SDK --mode agent)
 5 Post-packaging → staging E2E + multi-turn sim + human-eval (rovo-eval, ASE
   for human campaigns) 6a. Shadow / A-B → live traffic mirror + Switcheroo
   splits (rovo-eval online + ML Lens) 6b. Continuous → scheduled
   drift/calibration/fairness checks on prod sample (AIX-eval scheduled +
   ml_lens_query_client)

rovo-eval vs AIX-eval selection criteria (drawn directly from SPIKE: ML 
Evaluation Framework, page 6098222361, which recommends AIX-eval for TWG):
produced a deterministic decision tree keyed on stage, scope
(model|agent|skill), needs_prompt_optimization, needs_human_eval. AIX-eval
owns Stages 1–3 + 6b (Python flexibility, MLflow, prod data, ALPO);
rovo-eval/Stratus Evals SDK owns Stages 4–6a (native ConvoAI integration,
multi-turn sim, FF A/B). Both share MLflow as a results sink. ASE Web UI at
go/rovoeval reserved for ad-hoc smoke tests and human-eval campaigns API.

AI-Native Non-Negotiables (mandatory presence on every report — encoded as a
YAML checklist + validator):

 1 Categorized failures (not single accuracy)
 2 All slices (tenant tier, locale, surface, persona)
 3 Mean ± std over ≥3 seeds
 4 Full k-fold for tabular tasks
 5 Calibration (reliability diagram + ECE)
 6 Confidence intervals (bootstrap)
 7 Fairness slice deltas vs policy threshold

Validator must run pre-publication; missing items downgrade autonomy 🟢→🟡 and
require human escalation rather than silent omission.


Tool/MCP coverage: New tools required are aix_eval_runner and
rovo_eval_runner; existing MCPs (atlassian, slack, socrates, bitbucket,
google_drive, switcheroo) cover dataset query, artifact pinning, report
publishing, and ramp-flag inspection. Cross-skill handoffs documented to
ml_launch_review_gate (Stage 3 input), mle_stakeholder_reporting (Experiment
Report templates), drift_triggered_retraining (Stage 6b → SOP-1),
ml_incident_response (Stage 6a regression → SOP-3), and
symphony_orbit_governance (ORBIT context emission + autonomy gating). Known
gaps: no unified eval CLI; CI not first-class (needs bootstrap wrapper);
calibration requires predict_proba plumbing; fairness slicing requires
sensitive attributes.
