Bitbucket MCP — primary reuse for PR authoring: 8 sub-tools
(bitbucketWorkspace, bitbucketRepository, bitbucketRepoContent,
bitbucketPullRequest, bitbucketPipeline, bitbucketDeployment,
bitbucketEnvironment). Fully covers the GitOps-via-PR pattern:

 • bitbucketRepository(action=defaultReviewers, excludeCurrentUser=true) →
   pull required reviewers
 • bitbucketRepoContent → branch.create, files.get (read existing
   micros.yaml/spinnaker.yml/ai-gateway routes/manifest), commit.create
   (atomic file map write; strict "Name <email>" author format)
 • bitbucketPullRequest → create (with draft=true, reviewers=[{uuid}]),
   comment/comments, diff, approve, merge (with mergeStrategy,
   closeSourceBranch)
 • bitbucketPipeline → run (with target.ref_type/ref_name, selector,
   variables), step.log for build observation
 • bitbucketRepository(action=getReportForCommit/getReportAnnotationsForCommit
   ) → Sonar/Snyk quality gates
 • bitbucketDeployment is read-only — observation, not a deploy trigger

Gaps in Bitbucket MCP: no Tarot/TEAMServe/SageMaker/Spinnaker/Micros control
plane, no AI Gateway publish, no Micros schema validation, no status-check
polling primitive, no CODEOWNERS-required enforcement — SKILL must add these.

Switcheroo MCP — primary reuse for canary/A-B gating: search_template (always
first), create_gate (boolean rollout,
idType=tenantId/atlassianAccountId/stableID), create_experiment (encodes 50/50
via groups=["control","variant_a"]), get_change_details (poll rollout %),
search_changelog (audit). Gap: no mid-rollout ramp action — must delegate to
humans or add a REST helper.

Compass MCP — read-only discovery:
component_search(includeOnCallSchedules=true, includeDependsOn=true),
component_get_documentation, component_get_package_dependencies,
