Canonical source found: Atlassian's MLRC is a DTI Ecosystem (DTIE) program.
Key Confluence pages: DTIE/4818634684 (template), DTIE/3611920350 (proposal —
DRI Qinlong Luo, Review Committee Ashley Chin / Shuguang Zhang / Qinlong Luo,
2-week intake), DTIE/4821487095 (Confluence Edition Awareness worked example),
DTIE/1199272524 (predecessor "ML Production Checklist" rubric — cites Breck et
al. 2017 ML Test Score, 28 tests across data/model/infra/monitoring).

Checklist content: Two phases with ~22 Must-Have items:

 • Pre-Experiment (10): Project Poster, Design doc, Privacy review (opt→Must
   in PP), Fairness review (opt), Pre-analysis notebook, Model Validation,
   Feature-eng pipeline merged, Training pipeline merged, Offline eval w/
   baseline, Model registered.
 • Pre-Production (12+): Approved privacy review, Post-analysis notebook,
   Inference pipeline schema, Unit tests, Integration tests w/ consumer,
   Edge-case fallback, Rollback plan, Latency analysis, Retraining pipeline,
   Data/feature drift monitor, Inference + business metric monitor, Infra
   health monitor, Opsgenie+Slack alerts, Statsig+GASV3 setup, on-call
   runbook.

MCP coverage (~60-70% today): atlassian (Jira/Confluence
get/search/create/update/transitions), bitbucket (repo, file content, PRs,
pipelines), socrates (SQL for offline metrics), slack (alert channel), gmail
(datascience-ml-oncall@atlassian.com), google_calendar (review session),
switcheroo/compass (FF + component SLO). These cover PE-1 through PE-9 and
PP-1, PP-2, PP-4, PP-5, PP-6, PP-7 partially, PP-15.

Gaps requiring the new Subtask-2 tool: unified mlplatform.* MCP for MLflow
run/registry, Databricks job, Airflow/Argo DAG runs, Statsig experiment
config, Opsgenie policy, Helios drift monitor (KS/KL/cosine ≥0.60 thresholds),
Splunk/SignalFX observability dashboards. These cover PE-10 and PP-3, PP-8,
PP-9, PP-10, PP-11, PP-12, PP-13, PP-14.

5-phase gate design: (A) intake & artifact discovery → (B) Pre-Experiment
verify → (C) Pre-Production verify (parallel) → (D) score (per-item 0/0.5/1,
Breck 4-band ladder) & decide (Jira transition + PR comment + Slack) → (E)
generate filled review Confluence page + email committee + calendar review
slot.

Autonomy mapping (Symphony 3-tier / RFC-002 L1-L5): L1 read+post: fully
autonomous; L2 Jira transitions: autonomous on 100% pass; L3 merge/deploy
gate: warm-up human approval; L4-L5 rollback execution: always require human
confirmation (Agent Budget Guardrails).


Notable edge cases: Original DRI is deactivated (skill must resolve current
owner), per-team checklist variants exist, optional/Must-Have changes between
phases, fairness must be upgraded for models touching protected attrs,
Socrates calls are async (needs backoff), unknown-vs-fail must be
distinguished (no auto-pass on unknown).
