─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Key findings:


 1 Per-experiment budget enforcement is sourced from Agent Budget Guardrails 
   for Atlassian AI Systems (Confluence page 6907095043). The SOP encodes: (a)
   5-axis budget envelope (tokens, $, tool-calls, model invocations,
   duration); (b) soft warnings at 50/75/90% + hard kill-switch at 100%; (c) 4
   anomaly detectors (cost-vs-median, tool-call spike, token divergence,
   low-yield retries); (d) hierarchical policy defaults (use-case → team →
   org), where locals can lower but not exceed org bounds; (e) AI Gateway +
   ContextShield as dual enforcement points. Today's MCP coverage: socrates
   queries cost/median, slack+atlassian+gmail deliver warnings, bitbucket
   stores policy-as-code, atlassian writes audit logs. Gaps: no real-time
   kill-switch tool, no IDE/CLI warning hook — must call into Subtask-2 tools
   finops_cost_query, circuit_breaker_control, orbit_context_client.
 2 SageMaker → TEAMServe migration template sources are: [DRAFT] SageMaker to
   TeamServe Migration Master Guide (7081364303), Teamserve Cost Savings vs 
   SageMaker (6531298025), and QI Migration Plan & Inventory (7073104504).
   Headline economics: ~59% / ~$5.6M/yr saved across 33 models, 615 replicas,
   10 regions ($320K/mo vs $788K/mo effective; 730 hrs/mo basis). Top 3
   drivers: p5en.48xlarge (~$2.48M/yr), g5.2xlarge (~$1.68M/yr), g6e.xlarge
   (~$642K/yr). Important caveat: p5en estimate uses 0.4916 global discount
   ratio (only list pricing available); 24×7 replica assumption overstates
   savings for bursty workloads.
 3 3-step migration framework: Step 1 = artifact prep + ML Registry v3 (model
   owner); Step 2 = deploy to TeamServe in all 9 prod regions (TeamServe
   team); Step 3 = client cutover with dedicated *TeamServeClient per model
   (service owner).
 4 3-phase rollout per model: Shadow (parallel calls, log diffs, <1% semantic
   divergence) → Canary (1/5/25/50/100%, starting prod-west2, ≥24h soak each)
   → Cutover (flip across regions; retain SageMaker endpoint ≥2 weeks).
   Statsig flags: FF_QI_<MODEL>_TEAMSERVE_SHADOW/_CUTOVER. Monitoring parity
   via teamserve.inference.sli mirror of sagemaker.inference.sli.v2.
   Decommission removes SM_ENDPOINT_*, sageMaker.models YAML entries, old
   client code, unused flags.
 5 Tool coverage: bitbucket, atlassian, socrates, slack, gmail handle
   planning, inventory, PRs, audit, notifications, post-cutover cost
   validation. Gaps: no TeamServe deploy/Launchpad MCP, no ML Registry v3
   register MCP — needs Subtask-2 orbit_context_client, signalfx_detector_iac
   (parity detector), ml_lens_query_client (parity dashboard),
   finops_cost_query (savings validation), plus a recommended new TeamServe 
   deploy tool.
 6 Autonomy bands: 🟢 queries/inventory/soft warnings/audit; 🟡 budget
   escalation, per-canary ramp, PR creation, parity detector authoring; 🔴
   hard kill-switch and decommission (irreversible). All decisions emit audit
   rows per Policy for AI Agents in SDLC.
 7 Risks flagged: no realtime kill-switch tool exists; Master Guide is [DRAFT]
   (re-fetch each invocation); p5en cost estimate is approximate; no prior
   cost_and_capacity_stewardship/SKILL.md exists in the repo (greenfield
   authoring).
