─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Key findings:


 1 Per-experiment budget enforcement is sourced from Agent Budget Guardrails 
   for Atlassian AI Systems (Confluence page 6907095043). The SOP encodes: (a)
   5-axis budget envelope (tokens, $, tool-calls, model invocations,
   duration); (b) soft warnings at 50/75/90% + hard kill-switch at 100%; (c) 4
   anomaly detectors (cost-vs-median, tool-call spike, token divergence,
   low-yield retries); (d) hierarchical policy defaults (use-case → team →
   org), where locals can lower but not exceed org bounds; (e) AI Gateway +
   ContextShield as dual enforcement points. Today's MCP coverage: socrates
   queries cost/median, slack+atlassian+gmail deliver warnings, bitbucket
