─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Key findings:

 1 Production substrate (the shared cause): all four patterns are failure
   modes of the documented responsible-ai-api runtime topology — gunicorn (4
   workers, --timeout 60, --graceful-timeout 30) with gevent, co-located OTel
   collector + Statsig sidecars in a Micros WebServer CRD, autoscaled by KEDA
   (3..12 pods, CPU @ 58%, 300s stabilization), behind an ALB whose default
   deregistration_delay=300s is mismatched against gunicorn's 30s graceful
   timeout.
 2 Pattern catalogue (one detector + one diagnostic + one mitigation each):
    • OTel sidecar race — main container Ready before collector; telemetry gap
      masks errors. Mitigate via wait_for_otel_ready(), longer startupProbe,
      pre-warm.
    • Tenant burst — one tenant_id > 60% of mix saturates worker queue.
      Mitigate via per-tenant token-bucket + fail-open kill-switch (role-doc
      §5.3).
    • gevent saturation — workers blocked on slow downstream; p99↑, CPU low,
      KEDA does NOT scale. Mitigate via circuit-breaker @ 20%/60s (role-doc §6
      SOP-3), lower --timeout=30, AZ rotation, canary auto-rollback.
    • ALB decoupling — two modes: (a) ALB ships traffic to terminating pods
      (timeout mismatch); (b) shallow /healthcheck passes while deep health
      fails. Mitigate via aligning deregistration_delay, adding
      readinessGates, splitting /ready from /healthcheck, preStop: sleep 35.
 3 MCP coverage mapping — Slack notify, Jira CTSC incident CRUD/transitions,
   Bitbucket PR-for-config-fix, Confluence PIR, Socrates SQL diagnostics,
   Compass owner lookup, gmail/drive distribution are all covered today by the
   6 reused MCPs. Three Subtask-2 gaps: ml_lens_query_client (real-time PromQL
   — gunicorn/KEDA metrics), signalfx_detector_iac (detectors-as-code so the
   four runbook entries become standing alerts with runbook:<pattern> labels),
   and circuit_breaker_control (programmatic CB arm/disarm).
 4 SKILL deliverables specified: mandatory first-page symptom-to-pattern
   triage matrix; four SignalFx detector definitions (Python detect(when(...))
   form, each publishing runbook:<pattern> labels for JSM-Ops auto-routing);
   SLO anchors (Observability/Availability/Latency burn-rate windows per
   pattern); composed incident workflow (detector → JSM-Ops alert →
   label-driven SKILL branch → diagnostic → autonomy-gated mitigation →
   pir_drafter handoff).
 5 Autonomy gating per pattern maps to Symphony 3-tier × RFC-002 L1–L5: 🟢
   autonomous for queries/Slack/Jira/PR-draft/CB-arm (safety action); 🟡
   propose for prod config changes; 🔴 human-required for AZ rotation and
