## Original User Request
**Description**: Create skills and tools for the AI MLE's **Run, Evaluate, Govern & Communicate** surface — covering production observability/SLO engineering, incident response, drift-triggered retraining, evaluation frameworks, cost stewardship, Symphony/ORBIT governance, and stakeholder communication. SKILLS to create: (1) `ml_observability_and_slo` — encodes ML Lens drift queries (KS test, KL divergence, cosine ≥ 0.60 for NLP), SignalFx detectors-as-code authoring, per-endpoint SLO IaC, autoscaling tuning, circuit-breaker (20%/60s) maintenance per §2 R#1, §2 R#7, §4.3, §5.1; (2) `drift_triggered_retraining` — encodes SOP-1 end-to-end (drift signal → cross-correlation → reproduce baseline → parallel retrain → eval → register → propose-deploy → canary → ORBIT append) per §6 SOP-1; (3) `ml_incident_response` — encodes SOP-3 (circuit-breaker auto-activation, Slack ack-in-seconds, 30-min status cadence, cross-experiment root-cause correlation, PIR auto-draft within 5 BD with TTD/TTH/TTR/TTC) per §6 SOP-3, ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook, responsible-ai-api runbook; (4) `ml_evaluation_protocol` — encodes the 6-stage protocol (offline → adhoc → released → packaging → post-packaging → shadow/A/B → continuous) plus rovo-eval (multi-turn agent sim, ConvoAI) and AIX-eval (Pythonic, ML-Studio-native, prod-data, prompt optimization), and the AI-native non-negotiables (every failure case categorized, all slices reported, mean±std multi-seed, full k-fold, calibration + CIs + fairness) per §4.2, §10.2; (5) `ml_launch_review_gate` — automates ML Launch Review Checklist (privacy review, rollback plan, drift monitor, alerting) as gate per §4.1; (6) `cost_and_capacity_stewardship` — FinOps & ML Artifact Cost Monitoring queries, per-experiment budget enforcement, SageMaker→TEAMServe migration evaluation per §2 R#10, §4.3; (7) `symphony_orbit_governance` — Symphony 3-tier autonomy enforcement, ORBIT bootstrap/append, policy-pack compliance check, audit-trail emission, RFC-002 L1–L5 maturity gating per §2 R#9, §7.2, §10.5; (8) `mle_stakeholder_reporting` — auto-generates Model Cards, Architecture Comparison Reports, Experiment Reports (with equal-rigor negative results), Weekly Experiment Digest, Per-Incident PIR, Daily Standup Digest, Quarterly Impact Narrative per §4.4, §7.3, §9 (leverages existing atlassian/slack/google_drive/gmail MCPs). TOOLS to create: (a) `ml_lens_query_client` — drift, model-perf, system-health, data-quality dashboard queries; (b) `signalfx_detector_iac` — author/apply detectors-as-code; (c) `rovo_eval_runner` and (d) `aix_eval_runner` — programmatic eval execution; (e) `circuit_breaker_control` — activate/inspect circuit breakers; (f) `finops_cost_query` — ML Artifact Cost Monitoring queries; (g) `orbit_context_client` — read model lineage/experiment history/data-quality signals and write outcome enrichments; (h) `pir_drafter` — produces PIR from reasoning traces with TTD/TTH/TTR/TTC. Existing MCPs reused: `atlassian` (Confluence model cards, Jira incident tickets), `slack` (alerts/war-room), `google_drive`+`gmail` (distribution), `socrates` (data queries for drift/cost), `bitbucket` (rollback PRs). RESEARCH REQUIREMENT: study ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook, responsible-ai-api runbook (OTel sidecar race, tenant burst, gevent saturation, ALB decoupling), SPIKE: ML Evaluation Framework, MLOps@CoreML Long-Term Plan, Agent Budget Guardrails, Agentic Operations in the New SDLC, RFC-002, Policy for AI Agents in SDLC.

