─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Key findings:

 1 Lineage is a triangle anchored on MLflow. Every Tarot v3 model version must
   converge three edges: mlflow_run_uri (anchor), training_dataset_uri, and
   feature_views[]. The MLflow run_id UUID — not the Model_<TS> run name — is
   the canonical join key. artifacts/building_ml_models_vnext.txt already
   establishes this: production tables use model_version = MLflow run ID.
 2 Bidirectional handoff with the Build half is MLflow-mediated. Build emits
   an MLflow run with canonical params (dataset_uri, dataset_version,
   feature_table_uri, feature_table_version), artifacts (ablation matrix,
   logged model with signature, conda_env), and tags
   (architecture_comparison_uri, parent_tarot_model_version_id). Ship-side
   SKILL derives the Tarot v3 payload — never asks the user to author it.
   After register, the SKILL writes back tarot_model_version_id,
   tarot_registry_uri, tarot_replication_job_id, tarot_registered_at tags to
   the MLflow run to close the loop.
 3 Env-file pinning is strict and refuse-fail-closed. Required: conda_yaml
   (s3), pip_requirements (s3, ==-pinned only), dockerfile (digest-pinned
   @sha256:, or null), python_version (3-part), cuda_version (or null for
   CPU). SKILL must lint pins, cross-check Python/CUDA across files, and
   reject latest tags or >= specifiers.
 4 Input-schema format ranking: (1) mlflow.signature — default, auto-derived
   from mlflow.<framework>.log_model; (2) json-schema — Pydantic→Draft 2020-12
   for HTTP/gRPC Pydantic models; (3) avro — only for Kafka path. Always
   include a working example (used for replay-on-history shadow tests).
   Generative models need an augmented Pydantic wrapper schema; multi-modal
   models need both TensorSpec + JSON-Schema metadata.
 5 Pydantic-v2 validator in the SKILL. A TarotV3RegisterPayload model enforces
   every refuse-on-missing field (compliance.fairness_checks_passed,
   red_team_status, lineage.mlflow_run_uri, lineage.feature_views
   min_length=1, env s3:// scheme, input_schema.example non-empty), and
   short-circuits tenant_scope=cross to 🔴 escalation.
 6 MCP coverage confirmed gap. No existing MCP toolset writes to Tarot v3;
   tarot_registry_client is genuinely net-new (sibling workers 7 and 10
   confirm).
 7 SKILL workflow: trigger (Build tags candidate_for_ship=true) → preflight
   (verify Build contract) → compose → validate (Pydantic) → package →
   register → attach_env/input_schema/lineage → trigger_replication →
   round-trip back-write to MLflow → emit Confluence Model Card → update
   CTSC-39558.

Day-One Readiness rows contributed: MLflow tag-write on third-party runs;
Tarot v3 attach_lineage / attach_env / attach_input_schema scopes; Confluence
read for architecture-comparison verification; Symphony agent env vars
(SYMPHONY_AGENT_ID, POLICY_PACK_VERSION, ORBIT_CONTEXT_REF); packaged-artifact
S3 read for .pkl lint.

Open questions for aggregator: canonical Tarot v3 REST host; Tarot server-side
strictness vs. local-only enforcement; canonical MLflow tracking URI
normalization; Tecton-vs-MLFS URI schemes post-deprecation; safetensors_only
server-side check; attach_* idempotency semantics; cross-principal MLflow
ACLs.


