## Original User Request
**Description**: Create skills and tools for the AI MLE's **Model Build & Ship** lifecycle — covering training/experimentation, feature engineering, model registry/packaging, and serving/deployment. This subtask covers Atlassian platforms: Databricks, ML Studio, ML Fabric, MLflow, Optimus Prime HPO, Tecton, MLFS, Unity Catalog, ML Registry (Tarot v3), MSP SDK, Deployment Store, TEAMServe (gRPC/K8s/Triton), AWS SageMaker, AI Gateway, Launchpad, Spinnaker, Micros service descriptors, feature flags, and Bitbucket Pipelines. SKILLS to create: (1) `ml_experiment_lifecycle` — encodes SOP-2 (hypothesis → literature synthesis → pre-analysis → parallel design (5–10 variants) → mandatory ablations → multi-seed/k-fold/stratified CV → comprehensive error analysis → recommendation with rejected-alternatives) per §3.4, §4.2, §6 SOP-2, §10.2; (2) `feature_store_lifecycle` — defines/versions/audits features in Tecton/MLFS, runs coverage/freshness/sparsity audits per connector/region/tenant per §2 R#4, §4.3, §6 SOP-2 step 4; (3) `model_packaging_and_registration` — Tarot v3 registration with compliance metadata, env files, input schema, lineage per §2 R#5; (4) `deployment_manifest_and_rollout` — authors deployment manifests (intent, non-goals, invariants, risk class, test/rollback/monitoring plan) and runs canary/shadow/A/B with feature-flag gating per §2 R#6, §4.4, §10.5. TOOLS to create (only if no existing tool covers the operation): (a) `mlflow_run_manager` — programmatic run creation/logging with the standardized `Model_<TS>` name pattern, flattened params, per-segment metrics, framework artifact logging per §4.3; (b) `mlstudio_databricks_job_launcher` — schedule/launch training jobs, manage GPU quota, retrieve results; (c) `tecton_mlfs_client` — feature def/version/audit/coverage queries; (d) `tarot_registry_client` — register/fetch model artifacts with lineage; (e) `teamserve_sagemaker_deployer` — programmatic deploy/canary/rollback against TEAMServe gRPC endpoint pattern `grpc-teamserve-{region}.{env}.services.kitt-inf.net:443` and SageMaker endpoints; (f) `aigateway_router_config` — manage routing for OpenAI/Anthropic/Bedrock/Gemini/internal LLMs; (g) `spinnaker_micros_descriptor_editor` — service-descriptor edits with feature-flag gating. Existing Bitbucket MCP can be leveraged for PR authoring but NOT for ML platform APIs — those require new tools. RESEARCH REQUIREMENT: discover internal CLIs/SDKs/APIs for each platform (ML Studio One-Pager, MSP SDK docs, Building ML Models in vNext with MLflow, Feature Store Implementation Plan, Launchpad Pipelines doc, Optimus Prime HPO doc, responsible-ai-api codebase patterns for TEAMServe gRPC + SageMaker `ml.g5.xlarge` patterns).

**Todos**:
- Inventory all internal Atlassian platforms in scope (ML Studio, Databricks, ML Fabric, MLflow tracking URI, Tecton, MLFS, Unity Catalog, Tarot v3, MSP SDK, TEAMServe, SageMaker, AI Gateway, Launchpad, Spinnaker, Micros) and identify their SDKs/CLIs/REST APIs.
- For each TOOL listed, validate that no existing MCP toolset covers it; document the gap and propose the new tool surface (auth, key endpoints, primary operations).
- Author `ml_experiment_lifecycle` SKILL.md encoding SOP-2 with AI-native non-negotiables (multi-seed mean±std, full k-fold, mandatory ablations, exhaustive failure-case taxonomy, rejected-alternatives, literature synthesis).
- Author `feature_store_lifecycle` SKILL.md with proactive coverage/sparsity audit patterns referenced from §4.3 and §6 SOP-2 step 4.
- Author `model_packaging_and_registration` SKILL.md with Tarot v3 compliance metadata schema (env files, input schema, lineage).
- Author `deployment_manifest_and_rollout` SKILL.md with the non-negotiable manifest schema (intent + non-goals + invariants + risk + test/rollback/monitoring plans) and canary/shadow patterns including the 50/50 rollout and ~25–45 min cutover window from §9.
- Study `responsible-ai-api` codebase as the canonical pattern reference (two-stage LLaMA 3.1 8B → GPT-OSS Safeguard 20B prompt moderator, SageMaker→TEAMServe migration ~$5.6M/yr) and cite patterns in the skills.
- Specify Day-One Readiness tool-access matrix for each new tool (credentials, scopes, GPU quotas).
